    <solution><m>f(x,y,z)=c</m> gives a cylinder about the
<m>x</m>-axis, with radius <m>\sqrt{c}</m>, while setting <m>h(x,y,z) = c</m>
gives a cylinder about the <m>y</m>-axis, with radius <m>\sqrt{c}</m>.
Thus <m>f(x,y,z)</m> matches the level surfaces in
2, and <m>h(x,y,z)</m> matches the level
surfaces in 3.



